      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "CRM ACL Overview",
      "Anchor": "crm-acl-overview",
      "SectionPath": [],
      "Text": "Certain entities in your system may be visible to some users and not others. These security policies are represented as access control lists (ACLs) within LinkedIn.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "CRM ACL Overview",
      "Anchor": "crm-acl-overview",
      "SectionPath": [],
      "Text": "ACLs consist of 3 parts - atsEntityAcls, atsEntityAclAssignees, and record level settings that define whether ACLs apply. You will create atsEntityAcl records to associate your entities with security groups or roles in your system. Then, you\u0027ll create atsEntityAclAssignee records to associate your users with security groups or roles in your system for a specific entity type. Finally, you will define if ACLs are applicable on any record you sync to LinkedIn. These steps can happen in any order and ACL-restricted records will only be visible when all three elements are defined.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "CRM ACL Overview",
      "Anchor": "crm-acl-overview",
      "SectionPath": [],
      "Text": "Note",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "CRM ACL Overview",
      "Anchor": "crm-acl-overview",
      "SectionPath": [],
      "Text": "The latest API version is 202604. Use this version in the LinkedIn-Version header for all API requests to access the most recent features and improvements.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "table",
