    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Throttle Limits",
      "Anchor": "throttle-limits",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Throttle Limits"
      ],
      "Text": "The visibility of your customer\u0027s synced entities within LinkedIn products will depend on the ACLs you sync. Before syncing ACLs, there are a few steps you must complete:",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Throttle Limits",
      "Anchor": "throttle-limits",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Throttle Limits"
      ],
      "Text": "Bind the your users with LinkedIn Person IDs\nSync ACLs\nSync Restricted Records",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Throttle Limits",
      "Anchor": "throttle-limits",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Throttle Limits"
      ],
      "Text": "Details for each step are below.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "1. Bind your users with LinkedIn Person IDs",
      "Anchor": "1-bind-your-users-with-linkedin-person-ids",
      "SectionPath": [
        "1. Bind your users with LinkedIn Person IDs"
      ],
      "Text": "ACL assignees are LinkedIn members and represented by LinkedIn person IDs. LinkedIn Recruiter users, which are bound to LinkedIn member profiles, have LinkedIn person IDs that must be mapped to a CRM user if they are to leverage features of CRM Connect. You must implement a method to identify the person ID for each user using your integration so that ACLs can be defined.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "1. Bind your users with LinkedIn Person IDs",
      "Anchor": "1-bind-your-users-with-linkedin-person-ids",
      "SectionPath": [
        "1. Bind your users with LinkedIn Person IDs"
      ],
      "Text": "There are multiple ways that this can be accomplished:",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Bind through OAuth (preferred)",
      "Anchor": "bind-through-oauth-preferred",
      "SectionPath": [
        "1. Bind your users with LinkedIn Person IDs",
        "Bind through OAuth (preferred)"
      ],
      "Text": "Within your solution, you can send users through the OAuth2 authorization code grant flow to retrieve the LinkedIn person ID. See Bind CRM Users for more details on how this can be accomplished.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Match on email address with manual intervention",
      "Anchor": "match-on-email-address-with-manual-intervention",
      "SectionPath": [
        "1. Bind your users with LinkedIn Person IDs",
        "Match on email address with manual intervention"
      ],
      "Text": "Retrieve a list seat holders via the seatsV2 API. Using this list of seatholders, you can perform a match between the email address in your CRM and the email of the seatholder.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Match on email address with manual intervention",
      "Anchor": "match-on-email-address-with-manual-intervention",
      "SectionPath": [
        "1. Bind your users with LinkedIn Person IDs",
        "Match on email address with manual intervention"
      ],
      "Text": "Because this matching is not 100% accurate \u2014 there could be any number of reasons why a LinkedIn Recruiter seatholder has a different email address than the email populated in the CRM \u2014 you must but offer a way for administers to manually configure mappings when email resolution for a seatholder fails. This functionality can live within an administrative settings section for this integration in your UI.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "2. Sync ACLs",
      "Anchor": "2-sync-acls",
      "SectionPath": [
        "2. Sync ACLs"
      ],
      "Text": "You should sync ACLs in the following scenarios:",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "2. Sync ACLs",
      "Anchor": "2-sync-acls",
      "SectionPath": [
        "2. Sync ACLs"
      ],
      "Text": "During the historical data sync after a customer onboards\nWhen a secured entity is created, deleted, or its security info is modified in your system\nWhen a customer user is created, deleted, or its security info is modified in your system",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
